[statement]
Observed; the rule is not yet known in full. A package installed for its
condition, providing a name at no version without a priority, does not
answer that name where it was required before: `top` needs `c` and `y`,
and `x`, triggered by `y`, provides `c`; apk refuses `c`. Required only
after `x` is installed, `c` is answered by it.

[repository]
P:x
V:1
i:y
p:c

P:y
V:1

P:top
V:1
D:c y

[request]
top

[answer apk-tools 3.0.9-r0]
| ERROR: unable to select packages:
|   c (virtual):
|     note: please select one of the 'provided by'
|           packages explicitly
|     provided by: x
|     required by: top-1[c]
refused
